@startuml SMV_A4_1_1_AS_IS
' SOURCE: Arabic procedure A.4.1/1 and its flowchart (nine manual steps).
' This is NOT the proposed software workflow.
' ASIS-01..09 preserve the original flowchart steps.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #334155
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF7ED
skinparam SwimlaneTitleFontStyle bold

title A.4.1/1 - Small Vessel Registration (under 150 tons)\nAS-IS / Current Manual Procedure

|#E0F2FE|Applicant / Authorized Representative|
start
:Request registration of a vessel\nunder 150 tons [BR-001];
if (Applicant visits ministry first?) then (Yes)
  |#DCFCE7|Registration Officer|
  :Receive paper documents from owner\nor authorized representative [ASIS-01];
  :Review supporting documents [ASIS-02];
  while (Required documents incomplete?) is (Yes)
    :Suspend the transaction until\nmissing documents are supplied [BR-008];
    |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
    :Bring missing documents;
    |Registration Officer|
    :Review completed file [ASIS-02];
  endwhile (No)
  :Issue Small Vessel Inspection Form [ASIS-03];
  :Collect prescribed service fee,\nsurveyors' wages, and any violations [ASIS-04];
  |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
  :Take the documents for inspection\nat an external inspection center [ASIS-05];
else (No - direct center visit)
  |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
  :Go directly with required documents\nto an external inspection center [BR-005];
  |#FEF3C7|External Inspection Center / Flag State Control|
  :Receive documents and collect fees\nat the center [BR-005];
  note right
    Source note permits direct attendance
    with required documents and collection
    of fees at the external center.
    It does not specify an online booking.
  end note
endif

|External Inspection Center / Flag State Control|
:Inspect vessel and prepare inspection\nresults / completed inspection form [ASIS-05];
|Applicant / Authorized Representative|
:Return documents after inspection\nto the responsible officer [ASIS-06];
|Registration Officer|
:Review returned inspection paperwork;
:Prepare registration certificate [ASIS-07];
:Sign registration certificate [ASIS-07];
|#F3E8FF|Successive Responsible Officials|
:Apply subsequent signatures [ASIS-07];
|#FCE7F3|Ship Registrar|
:Sign registration certificate [ASIS-07];
|Registration Officer|
:Receive returned signed certificate [ASIS-08];
:Deliver certificate to applicant\nand retain one copy [ASIS-09];
|Applicant / Authorized Representative|
:Receive registration certificate;
stop

legend right
  **Confirmed source rules**
  [BR-001] Vessel is below 150 tons.
  [BR-002] Required documentation depends on the case:
             evidence of ownership; foreign-flag deletion
             certificate where applicable; purchase invoice;
             origin certificate; customs declaration;
             valid owner Civil ID; for companies, authorized
             signature and commercial registration;
             official POA for representation; MOC clearance.
  [BR-003] Service-fee table shows 16 fixed units.
             Surveyor wages and violations may also apply.
             Currency is NOT confirmed in supplied images.
  [BR-004] Published processing time: 2-3 working days.
  [BR-005] External-center-first alternative is allowed;
             that center collects fees in this route.
  [BR-006] Signatures: officer -> successive officials
             -> ship registrar.
  [BR-007] A copy of the certificate is retained.
  [BR-008] Missing documents suspend the procedure.
  [BR-009] Insurance document wording indicates validity
             after registration procedures; confirm timing.
  [BR-010] Official POA required when acting by proxy.
  [BR-011] Applicant returns inspected documents to officer.
  **Source metadata**
  Service frequency: daily.
  Service place: Kuwait Ports Authority building,
    Shuwaikh Industrial Area, first floor, office 105.
  The Coast Guard is named as an external participant,
    but no automatic Coast Guard transfer is shown.
endlegend

footer Source-based process model; confirm local terminology with service owner.
@enduml
@startuml SMV_A4_1_1_TO_BE
' Proposed digitization of service A.4.1/1.
' IMPORTANT: [ASIS-NN] is source mapping; [SYS-NN] denotes
' system functionality; [PROP-NN] requires ministry/client approval.
' The source does NOT establish e-payment, authentication provider,
' digital signatures, center API integration, or Coast Guard API.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #334155
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF7ED
skinparam SwimlaneTitleFontStyle bold
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam NoteBorderColor #D97706

title A.4.1/1 - Small Vessel Registration (under 150 tons)\nTO-BE / Proposed Digitized Service

|#E0F2FE|Applicant / Authorized Representative|
start
:Authenticate by configured identity mechanism\n[PROP-01];
:Create a new registration request [SYS-01];
|#EDE9FE|E-Service Portal|
:Create case ID and audit entry [SYS-02];
if (Intake channel?) then (Online ministry route)
  |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
  :Enter vessel, owner, and representation details;\nupload conditional supporting documents\n[ASIS-01 / SYS-03];
  |E-Service Portal|
  :Validate required fields, document presence,\nfile type/size, and tonnage < 150 [SYS-04];
  while (Submission complete?) is (No)
    :Mark NEEDS_INFORMATION;\nshow missing documents [BR-008 / SYS-05];
    |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
    :Supply / correct requested evidence;
    |E-Service Portal|
    :Revalidate submitted evidence [SYS-04];
  endwhile (Yes)
  |#DCFCE7|Registration Officer|
  :Review owner, vessel, and supporting file\n[ASIS-01 / ASIS-02];
  while (Officer accepts documentation?) is (No)
    :Request corrections with reason\n[BR-008 / SYS-06];
    |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
    :Provide corrected documents;
    |Registration Officer|
    :Verify corrected documents [ASIS-02];
  endwhile (Yes)
  :Approve initial file and issue\ninspection form [ASIS-03 / SYS-07];
  |E-Service Portal|
  :Assess prescribed fixed fee (16 units),\nsurveyor wages, and applicable violations\n[BR-003 / SYS-08];
  note right
    Currency, wage calculation and violation
    retrieval are configuration/integration
    decisions. Never hard-code unconfirmed
    payment amounts beyond the 16 source value.
  end note
  |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
  :Make electronic payment [PROP-02];
  |E-Service Portal|
  while (Payment confirmed?) is (No)
    :Remain AWAITING_PAYMENT;\nrecord failure or pending confirmation [SYS-09];
    |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
    :Retry / resolve payment;
    |E-Service Portal|
    :Verify receipt with payment provider [SYS-09];
  endwhile (Yes)
  :Issue unique receipt and inspection referral\n[PROP-02 / SYS-10];
  |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
  :Arrange and attend inspection\nwith referral and supporting file\n[ASIS-05];
else (External center first)
  |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
  :Attend permitted external center\nwith required documents [BR-005];
  |#FEF3C7|External Inspection Center|
  :Check necessary center-intake documents\nand collect applicable fees [BR-005];
  :Register or package center intake\nand fee receipt for ministry case [PROP-03];
  |E-Service Portal|
  :Link/create a unique case and payment record;\nflag fee as center-paid, pending verification\n[SYS-11];
  note right
    The original alternative goes directly to
    the external inspection center: ministry
    officer approval BEFORE inspection is not
    required by the supplied manual process.
    The officer validates the final file later.
  end note
endif

|External Inspection Center|
:Inspect vessel and record inspection outcome\n[ASIS-05 / SYS-12];
while (Vessel passed inspection?) is (No)
  :Record findings and reinspection need\n[PROP-04];
  |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
  :Rectify findings and arrange reinspection\n[PROP-04];
  |External Inspection Center|
  :Repeat inspection [PROP-04];
endwhile (Yes)
:Finalize signed inspection report [SYS-12];
if (Approved inspection-center integration?) then (Yes)
  :Submit authenticated inspection report\nelectronically [PROP-05];
  |E-Service Portal|
  :Attach inspection report to case [SYS-13];
else (No - manual fallback)
  |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
  :Return inspected documents to officer\n[ASIS-06 / BR-011];
  |Registration Officer|
  :Verify originals / received inspection result\nand add documents to case [SYS-13];
endif

|Registration Officer|
:Review inspection outcome, identity, ownership,\ncompleted file and fee evidence [SYS-14];
while (Final file is acceptable?) is (No)
  :Request corrections, with recorded reason\n[PROP-06];
  |Applicant / Authorized Representative|
  :Complete requested corrections;
  |Registration Officer|
  :Recheck updated file [SYS-14];
endwhile (Yes)

repeat
  |E-Service Portal|
  :Generate or revise draft registration certificate\nand proposed registration number [SYS-15];
  note right
    Registry numbering authority, reservation,
    uniqueness, and issuance timing need approval.
    Draft must not count as issued certificate.
  end note
  |Registration Officer|
  if (Officer accepts draft?) then (Yes)
    :Sign certificate draft [ASIS-07 / PROP-07];
    |#F3E8FF|Successive Responsible Officials|
    if (All successive officials approve?) then (Yes)
      :Sign in configured order [ASIS-07 / PROP-07];
      |#FCE7F3|Ship Registrar|
      if (Registrar approves?) then (Yes)
        :Apply final signature [ASIS-07 / PROP-07];
        |E-Service Portal|
        :Mark signatures complete [SYS-16];
      else (No)
        :Record registrar comments [PROP-07];
      endif
    else (No)
      :Record responsible official comments [PROP-07];
    endif
  else (No)
    :Record officer comments [PROP-07];
  endif
backward:Revise certificate / file and restart\nrequired signatures [PROP-07];
repeat while (All required signatures obtained?) is (No) not (Yes)

|E-Service Portal|
:Mark signed certificate ready for release;\nstore verification details [SYS-16];
|Registration Officer|
:Receive approved certificate\n[ASIS-08];
:Release certificate to applicant\n[ASIS-09 / SYS-17];
|E-Service Portal|
fork
  :Archive full case, approvals, fee receipts,\ncertificate and retained copy\n[ASIS-09 / BR-007 / SYS-18];
fork again
  :Notify applicant by configured channel\n[PROP-08];
fork again
  :Open post-registration insurance follow-up\nif policy confirms applicable timing\n[BR-009 / PROP-09];
end fork
|Applicant / Authorized Representative|
:Download or collect certificate\n[ASIS-09 / SYS-17];
stop

legend right
  **Source-grounded controls**
  BR-001: Only vessels below 150 tons.
  BR-002: Conditional documentation by ownership,
     foreign flag, applicant category and representation.
  BR-003: Fixed amount 16 (currency TBD), plus surveyor
     wages and violations where applicable.
  BR-004: Published 2-3 business days (no confirmed
     exclusion for inspection waiting time).
  BR-005: Direct external center and center fee collection.
  BR-006: Officer -> responsible officials -> ship registrar.
  BR-007: Preserve one copy of issued certificate.
  BR-008: Incomplete file is suspended until completed.
  BR-009: Insurance-after-registration wording; confirm timing.
  BR-010: Official power of attorney for a proxy.
  BR-011: Original post-inspection paperwork return.
  **Approval required before production**
  PROP-01: Identity provider and user onboarding.
  PROP-02: Payment gateway, currency, refunds, reconciliation.
  PROP-03: Center case intake and center receipt verification.
  PROP-04: Reinspection workflow / rejection policy.
  PROP-05: Center electronic signing and API integration.
  PROP-06: Post-inspection correction handling.
  PROP-07: Digital signature validity and rejection behavior.
  PROP-08: Notification methods and message templates.
  PROP-09: Insurance timing and post-registration enforcement.
  Coast Guard data sharing: separate approval; NOT automatic.
endlegend

footer Proposed TO-BE workflow. Validate all PROP decisions with service owner.
@enduml
@startuml SMV_A4_1_1_STATUS
' Proposed implementation state machine. All transitions require
' authorization and an immutable audit event. State IDs are stable API values.
' Center-first intake can include validated payment and inspection evidence.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}

title A.4.1/1 - Proposed Case Lifecycle / State Machine

[*] --> DRAFT : createCase
DRAFT --> SUBMITTED : submitOnline / importCenterCase
SUBMITTED --> INITIAL_REVIEW : intakeAccepted
INITIAL_REVIEW --> NEEDS_INFORMATION : requestMissingEvidence
NEEDS_INFORMATION --> INITIAL_REVIEW : resubmitEvidence
INITIAL_REVIEW --> AWAITING_PAYMENT : officeRouteValidated
AWAITING_PAYMENT --> AWAITING_INSPECTION : paymentVerified
INITIAL_REVIEW --> AWAITING_INSPECTION : centerFeeReceiptVerified
INITIAL_REVIEW --> FINAL_REVIEW : centerFileAndReportVerified

AWAITING_INSPECTION --> INSPECTION_IN_PROGRESS : inspectionBegins
INSPECTION_IN_PROGRESS --> REINSPECTION_REQUIRED : failedInspection [PROP-04]
REINSPECTION_REQUIRED --> INSPECTION_IN_PROGRESS : inspectionRebooked [PROP-04]
INSPECTION_IN_PROGRESS --> AWAITING_INSPECTION_REPORT : passedInspection
AWAITING_INSPECTION_REPORT --> FINAL_REVIEW : validatedInspectionReportReceived

FINAL_REVIEW --> NEEDS_INFORMATION : requestPostInspectionCorrections [PROP-06]
FINAL_REVIEW --> CERTIFICATE_DRAFT : finalFileApproved
CERTIFICATE_DRAFT --> OFFICER_SIGNATURE : draftGenerated
OFFICER_SIGNATURE --> SUPERVISOR_SIGNATURE : officerSigned
SUPERVISOR_SIGNATURE --> SUPERVISOR_SIGNATURE : nextSupervisorSigned [if more officials]
SUPERVISOR_SIGNATURE --> REGISTRAR_SIGNATURE : allRequiredOfficialsSigned
REGISTRAR_SIGNATURE --> READY_FOR_RELEASE : registrarSigned
OFFICER_SIGNATURE --> CERTIFICATE_DRAFT : returnedForCorrection [PROP-07]
SUPERVISOR_SIGNATURE --> CERTIFICATE_DRAFT : returnedForCorrection [PROP-07]
REGISTRAR_SIGNATURE --> CERTIFICATE_DRAFT : returnedForCorrection [PROP-07]
READY_FOR_RELEASE --> COMPLETED : officerReleasedCertificate
COMPLETED --> [*]

DRAFT --> WITHDRAWN : applicantWithdraws [PROP-10]
SUBMITTED --> WITHDRAWN : authorizedWithdrawal [PROP-10]
NEEDS_INFORMATION --> WITHDRAWN : authorizedWithdrawal [PROP-10]
WITHDRAWN --> [*]

note right of INITIAL_REVIEW
  For center-first route, never skip fee
  verification. If the source center has
  already performed inspection, require a
  verified report before FINAL_REVIEW.
end note

note bottom of COMPLETED
  After completion, insurance follow-up may
  continue in a separate compliance process
  only if BR-009 policy is confirmed.
  Coast Guard sync is not assumed.
end note

legend right
  All status changes require RBAC + audit trail.
  Payment confirmations must be idempotent.
  Signature order must be enforced server-side.
  Returned approval must invalidate downstream
    draft signatures as legally required (TBD).
  Applicant withdrawal is proposed, not sourced.
  SLA: published 2-3 working days; exclude only
    pauses confirmed by ministry policy.
endlegend
@enduml
@startuml SMV_A4_1_1_ARCHITECTURE
' Illustrative architecture only. Reuse existing project stack.
' External services are ports/adapters, not approved dependencies.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam PackageBorderColor #94A3B8

title Small Vessel Registration - Proposed Application Boundaries\n(Reference architecture, not procurement decision)

actor "Applicant / Representative" as Applicant
actor "Registration Officer" as Officer
actor "Successive Officials" as Supervisors
actor "Ship Registrar" as Registrar
actor "External Inspection Center" as Center

package "Digital Channels" {
  [Applicant Portal\nArabic / English, RTL] as UI
  [Staff Back Office\nReview and Signature Queues] as Backoffice
}

package "Application Backend" {
  [Identity / RBAC] as IAM
  [Registration Case API] as API
  [Workflow & State Transition Service] as WF
  [Document Validation & Storage Adapter] as Docs
  [Fees and Payment Ledger] as Fees
  [Inspection Handling Adapter] as Inspection
  [Certificate Generator and Approval Chain] as Certificate
  [Audit / Notifications / SLA] as Audit
}

database "Relational Database\n(Cases, statuses, approvals, fees)" as DB
cloud "Encrypted Object Storage\n(Documents, reports, certificates)" as Storage

package "Optional integrations - APPROVAL REQUIRED" {
  [Identity provider] as IdP
  [Payment provider] as Pay
  [Inspection center API] as CenterAPI
  [SMS / Email provider] as Notify
  [Coast Guard exchange] as CG
}

Applicant --> UI
Officer --> Backoffice
Supervisors --> Backoffice
Registrar --> Backoffice
Center --> CenterAPI : If approved / available
UI --> API
Backoffice --> API
API --> IAM
API --> WF
WF --> Docs
WF --> Fees
WF --> Inspection
WF --> Certificate
WF --> Audit
API --> DB
WF --> DB
Docs --> Storage
Certificate --> Storage
IAM ..> IdP : optional
Fees ..> Pay : optional
Inspection ..> CenterAPI : optional
Audit ..> Notify : optional
WF ..> CG : separate approval only

note bottom of WF
  Enforce server-side business rules and
  transitions; every transition produces
  an immutable audit event. Treat AS-IS rules
  as baseline and proposed digital services
  as configurable, separately approved options.
end note

@enduml
